My understanding is that a straight-forward extension is possible but
undesirable since you'd end up with large object files.  If you
compare the output of "ls -l" of any non-stripped ECOFF file with the
output of "size", I have no problem buying this argument.  It looks
like ECOFF debugging and possibly relocation information takes up
quite some space.  And don't say diskspace is free---something has to
produce, link, and write those object files and, for example, BFD does
everything incore, AFAIK.

Having ELF draft standard available would be a big plus.  Almost
anything would be better than the current situation.

