Subject: Re: Benchmarks (fwd)
In-Reply-To: <199603190417.UAA01815@proto.math.ucdavis.edu>

> Looks pretty favorable to the alpha to me.  I suspect gcc on alpha
> does better then gcc on pentium (relative to the tuned spec compilers),
> especially since the alpha has many more registers.

Actually, in terms of relative ideal optimized code quality,
the i386 gcc produces better code than alpha gcc.

This is primarily due to the fact that gcc does not yet really
understand how to schedule instructions through multiple pipelines
simultaneously.  I'm told this is being worked on, but I have
no idea if it is to be included in 2.8.

r~

