Subject: Re: booting Linux from ARC

Hi All,

Thanks for your advice, my friend and I were able to get MILO up and Linux
installed on my alphastation 200.  More questions though:

What happened to "dip" in Redhat 2.1 for the DEC Alpha?
It exists in Redhat 2.1 for Intel (/usr/sbin/dip), but we can't
find it in the Alpha version of Redhat.  Is there an equivalent tool for
connecting to a SLIP account?

Also does anyone one know how to do an Xconfiguration for use with a
ZLXp-E1 card?

Dave

From ewt@redhat.com Wed Mar 20 12:52:24 1996
Message-ID: <199603201727.JAA26280@nic.cerf.net>
Date: Wed, 20 Mar 1996 12:52:24 -0500 (EST)
From: Erik Troan <ewt@redhat.com>
Subject: Re: booting Linux from ARC
In-Reply-To: <199603201727.JAA26280@nic.cerf.net>

On Wed, 20 Mar 1996, David Bernstein wrote:

> What happened to "dip" in Redhat 2.1 for the DEC Alpha?
> It exists in Redhat 2.1 for Intel (/usr/sbin/dip), but we can't
> find it in the Alpha version of Redhat.  Is there an equivalent tool for
> connecting to a SLIP account?

dip needed patching, and the patches weren't available when 2.1 was
ready. There is a dip package in the devel tree on ftp.redhat.com which
is completely untested.

Erik

