>>>>> On Thu, 21 Mar 1996 14:56:16 +0000, Richard Black <Richard.Black@cl.cam.ac.uk> said:

  Richard> 2. rdfpcr and wrfpcr. Its less obvious to me what I do about those.

They read and write the floating point control register (fpcr).  They
are in arch/alpha/kernel/head.S.  Either you have a (very) old version
of head.S, an old version of head.o, or it failed to compile (which
would be strange).

	--david

